_tsi_primitives.dl7"}, 139 ],"f":"reader_node"},  {"a":"prelude/5_tsi_primitives.dl7"}, 961, 962, 66, 8, 66, 9 ],"f":"source"} ]},"input":"; One empty product per primitive class a foreign type stream can name.\n; `tsi.primitive(Id, Class)` binds the foreign id to the product declared\n; here, so two languages spelling the same class share one node identity.\n\n; TypeScript classes.\n(: string (* ))\n\n(: number (* ))\n\n(: boolean (* ))\n\n(: bigint (* ))\n\n(: symbol (* ))\n\n(: void (* ))\n\n(: undefined (* ))\n\n(: null (* ))\n\n(: never (* ))\n\n(: unknown (* ))\n\n; The `any` class is absent on purpose: `any` is one of the four names\n; `1_checker.pl:298-301` pins as a primitive, and a prelude edge of that name\n; shadows it for every program. The loader reports the class as absent.\n\n; Rust builtins.\n(: i8 (* ))\n\n(: i16 (* ))\n\n(: i32 (* ))\n\n(: i64 (* ))\n\n(: i128 (* ))\n\n(: u8 (* ))\n\n(: u16 (* ))\n\n(: u32 (* ))\n\n(: u64 (* ))\n\n(: u128 (* ))\n\n(: f32 (* ))\n\n(: f64 (* ))\n\n(: bool (* ))\n\n(: char (* ))\n\n(: str (* ))\n\n(: usize (* ))\n\n(: isize (* ))\n\n; Rust names this primitive class `unit` on the TSI wire.\n(: () (* ))\n","path":"prelude/5_tsi_primitives.dl7"}